# Public keys trusted to sign commits, for local verification.
# Referenced by gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile in env/.gitconfig; deployed to
# ~/.ssh/allowed_signers. Public key material only — safe to track.
#
# Principals are matched against the *committer email*, so every key lists both
# addresses in use. To verify: git log --show-signature
#
# Keep in sync with the SSH signing keys registered on github.com/settings/keys —
# a key here but not on GitHub verifies locally and shows "Unverified" on GitHub.
# All four below are currently registered there, so every commit in this repo's
# history verifies on both sides.
#
# Keys are named by machine, not by "this machine" — the file is shared, so whose
# machine is "this" depends on who last edited it. Match a line to a machine with
# its fingerprint: ssh-keygen -lf ~/.ssh/<key>.pub

